(* README *)

1 - Summary
    -------

    L002 formalizes a mirror obstruction over M001 checked derivability.
    For a regulator `M`, context `Gamma`, and formula `chi`, it separates:

      - a full negation fixed point, which derives `Bot`; and
      - a one-way mirror position `formula_negation chi -> chi`, which is
        compatible with consistency but excludes adequate recognition.

    The live core is:

      ExternalMirrorPosition M Gamma chi /\
      MirrorConsistent M Gamma

      implies

      AsIF M Gamma chi /\
      ~ CodedRecognitionAccepted M Gamma chi.

    Here `AsIF` means only that `M` has no checked derivation of
    `formula_negation chi`. It is not truth, belief, agency, or control.
    Acceptance is kept separate: accepted coded evidence re-enters `M` as a
    derivation of the negation that `AsIF` excludes.

    The world/brain/model layer makes relative consistency explicit. A
    `WorldBrainModelFrame` derives brain consistency from world soundness and
    transports it to model consistency through
    `ModelConsistentRelativeToBrain`. Model-to-world soundness remains a
    separate premise.

    A `ControlQuestion` packages a formula with its mirror witness. A
    consistent model cannot return the explicit negative verdict. If a binary
    decision is required, the remaining internal verdict is positive. If the
    world refutes that verdict and the model is world-sound, the binary
    specification is impossible.

    `RecursiveControlProcess` adds `yes`, `no`, and `reenter` responses over
    finite mirror iterates. Consistency excludes `no` at every depth. For each
    finite bound, either `yes` occurs within the bound or every stage through
    it is re-entry. The unbounded disjunction requires the explicit
    `ControlOutcomeDecidable` premise.


2 - Theorem Shape
    -------------

    Full fixed point:

      ExternalFixedPoint M Gamma chi
        -> regulator_theory_checked_derivable M Gamma Bot

    Live mirror:

      ExternalMirrorPosition M Gamma chi
        -> MirrorConsistent M Gamma
        -> AsIF M Gamma chi

      ExternalMirrorPosition M Gamma chi
        -> MirrorConsistent M Gamma
        -> ~ CodedRecognitionAccepted M Gamma chi

    Control question:

      MirrorConsistent M Gamma
        -> ~ ControlAnswersNo M Gamma question

      MirrorConsistent M Gamma
        -> BinaryControlDecision M Gamma question
        -> ControlAnswersYes M Gamma question

    Recursive control:

      forall fuel,
        (exists depth,
           depth <= fuel /\ ControlAnswersYesAt process depth) \/
        ReentersThrough process fuel

      ControlOutcomeDecidable process
        -> EventuallyAnswersYes process \/ ReentersForever process

    The first recursive statement is constructive. The second exposes the
    additional decision premise needed to pass from every finite bound to one
    unbounded disjunction.


